<p>Israeli airstrikes hit multiple locations in Lebanon on Sunday. Lebanon&#x27;s health ministry said seven people were killed in Kfarhata in the south, including a 4-year-old child, and four more were killed in Beirut&#x27;s Jnah neighbourhood, where 39 others were injured. Other reports put the nationwide death toll for the day at at least 14 or 15, as strikes and shelling stretched from Beirut south toward areas including Tyre. The attacks came after Israeli evacuation warnings, including an overnight order for residents to leave Kfarhata and a separate warning for the Masnaa border crossing with Syria, which later closed after the threat of attack. Israel&#x27;s military said it was stepping up operations against Hezbollah, while Hezbollah also fired projectiles toward northern Israel as fighting spread across the frontier.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/eZKUwewdC8kGRFCDS3w5_MLMfWu7JjJoeiEPzqCNxXah--vKA3V6fG3bNK5STCOmHKYsodD3acQ_Ez8Tw-avaNFLvBWG_fM-Ey6kOyzB-U__' alt='An apartment building destroyed in an Israeli airstrike in Beirut’s southern suburbs on Sunday.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Capital strikes: Lebanon&#x27;s state media said Israeli warplanes carried out eight airstrikes on Beirut&#x27;s southern suburbs during the day, underscoring how widely the bombardment had spread beyond a single neighbourhood.</li><li>Army casualty: The Lebanese army said an Israeli strike in southern Lebanon killed one of its soldiers earlier Sunday, showing the fighting also reached state forces.</li><li>Naval claim: Hezbollah said it fired a cruise missile at an Israeli warship off the coast, but the Israeli military said it was not aware of such an incident.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Israeli military: Lieutenant General Eyal Zamir said Israel would continue what he described as precise operations to degrade Hezbollah&#x27;s capabilities, strengthen defenses, and keep threats away from northern communities. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1988895/11-killed-in-israeli-airstrikes-in-lebanon'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>Lebanon&#x27;s health ministry: The ministry gave the death toll and injury figures from the Kfarhata and Jnah strikes, including the killing of a young child and dozens of people wounded in Beirut. (<a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/04/least-11-killed-israeli-airstrikes-lebanon-easter-sunday'>Al-Monitor</a>)</li><li>Hezbollah: The group said it fired projectiles at northern Israel and claimed a cruise missile attack on an Israeli warship off the coast as hostilities escalated. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/israel-renews-strikes-on-lebanon-several-killed-on-april-5-2026/article70827605.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1988895/11-killed-in-israeli-airstrikes-in-lebanon'>11 killed in Israeli airstrikes in Lebanon</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/middle-east/article/3349099/israeli-strikes-kill-11-lebanon-israel-announces-security-buffer'>Israeli strikes kill 11 in Lebanon, Israel announces ‘security buffer’</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/video/newsfeed/2026/4/5/israeli-air-strikes-shelling-across-lebanon-add-to-rising-death-toll'>Israeli air strikes, shelling across Lebanon add to rising death toll</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/israel-renews-strikes-on-lebanon-several-killed-on-april-5-2026/article70827605.ece'>Israel renews strikes on Lebanon, killing at least 11</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/04/06/israel-renews-lebanon-strikes-forcing-syria-border-crossing-to-close_6752146_4.html'>Israel renews Lebanon strikes, forcing Syria border crossing to close</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/04/israel-renews-lebanon-strikes-forces-syria-border-crossing-closed'>Israel renews Lebanon strikes, forces Syria b